# Keep the build context lean. The Dockerfile only consumes the server +
# shared workspaces; everything below is either dev tooling, build
# artifacts (regenerated inside the image), or sibling apps we don't
# ship as part of the server image.

# Dependencies + build artifacts (regenerated in-image)
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/out
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/.swc
**/.rollup.cache
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Test + coverage
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
**/bench-results

# Local env files (server reads env from Railway, not files)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Sibling tools / examples / top-level docs NOT shipped by any image.
# `apps/` is NOT excluded -- the unified Dockerfile builds dashboard
# and docs from there based on the WORKSPACE build arg.
examples
tools
# Top-level docs/ folder (not apps/docs which is the Nextra app).
/docs

# Prisma migrations history is kept (under packages/server/prisma); the
# local migration_lock dev artifact stays too -- Prisma needs it.

# IDE / VCS noise
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Loop / scratch infra (local-only)
.loop
PROMPT.txt
CONTRIBUTING.md
SECURITY.md
README.md
LICENSE
biome.json
scripts
.claude
